 "dates": "Thursday, January 14 – Sunday, January 17, 2010",
 "logline": "Four days in January: a partner till May, a novel about a man who kept quiet, the Saints on one big screen with everybody at one table, and a light left on at three-thirty.",
 "previously": [
  {
   "text": "Lena, from New Orleans, about the playoff game: “I’m watching it in the Fishbowl, and y’all are going to be quiet, and nobody is going to say anything to me till it’s over.”"
  },
  {
   "text": "Crossing the lawn toward the Haiti table, Laney: “Well. Somebody hand me my good manners. I’m fixing to need every one of them.”"
  },
  {
   "text": "Theo took one of Julian’s flyers. “Songs for Haiti. How many are about her?” Julian: “One.”"
  },
  {
   "text": "At the table, Lena: “No pictures at the table, please.” You: “It’s twenty dollars, Lena.”"
  },
  {
   "text": "At the front desk, Lena: “Skye’s envelope was the biggest. Tell her thank you. From Newman.” Skye wrote back: *tell her youre welcome. from me*",
   "if": "s2e4_relay==\"candor\""
  },
  {
   "text": "At the front desk, Lena: “Skye’s envelope was the biggest. Tell her thank you. From Newman.”",
   "if": "s2e4_relay!=\"candor\""
  },
  {
   "text": "On the porch swing on Del Playa, Skye: “I want to take you inside. I want that a lot. And I’m too sad tonight to be any good at it.” Then: “Saturday.”",
   "if": "s2e4_where==\"hers\""
  },
  {
   "text": "Under the streetlight on Ocean Road, Skye: “I want to take you home. I want that a lot. And I’m too sad tonight to be any good at it.” Then: “Saturday.”",
   "if": "s2e4_where!=\"hers\""
  }
